  "question": {
    "text": "<p>Suppose the gravitational force varies inversely as the <math><msup><mrow><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mi>h</mi></mrow></msup></math> power of the distance. Then the time period of a planet in circular orbit of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math>&nbsp;around the sun will be proportional to</p>\r",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
